{
  "id": 473820178,
  "iid": 24372,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: LZ* compression types optimization",
  "description": "Call wmem_array_grow before doing a long append. This does one realloc\ninstead of many, and also removes the need to use wmem_array_try_index\nand do an intermediate copy of a byte instead of copying directly from\nthe array.\n\nWhen we can copy multiple bytes at a time, do so.\n\nUse an unsigned value and subtract for match_offset in LZHUFF, instead\nof a signed integer that is multiplied by -1.\n\nWe have sample files in the tests that run on these compression types,\nand they work (they have non match lengths greater than 1). This also\nmakes the example in #21127 get to the point of wmem array failing\nallocation much, much faster if the bounds recently added are removed.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-14T14:28:38.799Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-14T23:52:10.363Z",
